{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":52.220001220703125,"text":"Building began in 1163 and took almost 200 years, which means nobody who laid the first stones lived to see it finished. Its two towers are 69 meters high, and its three round windows, the rose windows, glow like enormous flowers made of colored glass. Around the roof crouch the gargoyles, stone monsters with open mouths. They are neither decoration nor scarecrows, they are drainpipes. Rainwater runs through them and is thrown clear of the walls, because water running down stone is the worst enemy an old building has. In April 2019, a fire destroyed the roof and the spire. It did not fall. It was rebuilt by hundreds of carpenters, stonecutters, and glassworkers, and it opened again at the end of 2024.","words":[{"word":"Building","start":0,"end":0.6600000262260437},{"word":"began","start":0.6600000262260437,"end":1.2000000476837158},{"word":"in","start":1.2000000476837158,"end":1.5},{"word":"1163","start":1.5,"end":2.5399999618530273},{"word":"and","start":2.5399999618530273,"end":3.180000066757202},{"word":"took","start":3.180000066757202,"end":3.4000000953674316},{"word":"almost","start":3.4000000953674316,"end":3.859999895095825},{"word":"200","start":3.859999895095825,"end":4.579999923706055},{"word":"years","start":4.579999923706055,"end":5.139999866485596},{"word":"which","start":5.699999809265137,"end":5.78000020980835},{"word":"means","start":5.78000020980835,"end":6.019999980926514},{"word":"nobody","start":6.019999980926514,"end":6.5},{"word":"who","start":6.5,"end":6.800000190734863},{"word":"laid","start":6.800000190734863,"end":6.960000038146973},{"word":"the","start":6.960000038146973,"end":7.159999847412109},{"word":"first","start":7.159999847412109,"end":7.539999961853027},{"word":"stones","start":7.539999961853027,"end":7.960000038146973},{"word":"lived","start":7.960000038146973,"end":8.4399995803833},{"word":"to","start":8.4399995803833,"end":8.619999885559082},{"word"